Vlad Popescu wrote:

> I have tried praying at the altar, but I usually end up getting my god angry.

You shouldn't pray too much, or your god *will* get angry. You can
safely pray, however, if it's been a long time since you last prayed,
and you can greatly reduce that time by being nice to your god. :)

> Sacrificing a jackal corpse also didn't do much (I tried this only once,
> worshipping Kos). While reading this newsgroup, I have come across the concept
> of converting an altar. How can one do that and what are the benefits?

Basically, whenever you sacrifice something on an alter that does not
belong to your god (don't do this if there's a priest around) the two
gods will fight over the sacrifice, and unless your god is angry with
you there's a chance that he claims this altar as his own.

There's some monsters that are special when it comes to sacrifice, and
it might be a bad idea to #offer those.

Hint: In certain creatures, alignment and colour are connected.
Hint: Also, what your god dislikes you to eat, he'll dislike you to
#offer.

> Onward to statues... I have absolutely no idea what to do with them. Any hints
