Hint: Or ask your local dwarves for help.

> When I stumble upon a fountain or sink, I drink from it (not the smartest thing
> to do most of the time). What else can I do with them?

You can also (Alt-d)ip something into them. It's still dangerous, but
there are cases where it's beneficial.

This Oracle you asked about lives on a level where there's lots of
statues and a couple of fountains. You can #chat to her, pay the
(large) fee and get some cryptic information that might help you
playing even without spoilers. Write it down, as you're unlikely to
understand it right away.

> Finally, I end up losing or accidentally killing my pet most of the time
> (actually quite heartbreaking, beacause I named the cat after my real-life pet
> cat). How can I 'train' pets (so I've read around the newsgroup).

You can use magic to acquire new pets, or you can tame them in the
traditional way (dogs and cats will do anything for food).

